WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.533
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:04.848
- [Narrator] This is
the Fiji Banded Iguana,

00:00:04.848 --> 00:00:07.931
a creature as stunning as it is rare.

00:00:09.202 --> 00:00:12.268
Native to the tiny Fiji
Islands in the South Pacific,

00:00:12.268 --> 00:00:13.937
it is one of the most geographically

00:00:13.937 --> 00:00:17.152
isolated iguanas in the world.

00:00:17.152 --> 00:00:19.591
Vibrant like a jewel, these
reptiles are considered

00:00:19.591 --> 00:00:23.123
a national treasure by
the government of Fiji.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.845
Their emerald green colored
skin is sensitive to light

00:00:25.845 --> 00:00:28.699
and can change color to
match its background.

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:32.113
The males like this one are
banded with blue streaks.

00:00:32.113 --> 00:00:36.223
Their long, spiny toes end
in claws to help them climb,

00:00:36.223 --> 00:00:39.065
but none of these adaptations
can protect this species

00:00:39.065 --> 00:00:41.420
from the many threats it faces.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.047
Habitat loss from development,

00:00:43.047 --> 00:00:44.849
poaching for the illegal pet trade,

00:00:44.849 --> 00:00:48.792
and introduced predators like
rats, cats, and mongooses,

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:51.623
all cloud this creature's future.

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:54.206
This is the Fiji Banded Iguana.

